        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-06T13:42:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of creating this object and seeing if it throws, why not just add a \"static boolean supportsVersion()\" method to ApfGenerator?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1185,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1185,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "d6846a0d80e82ac22a81b8d0426b2216386f60e5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13cdfdeb_5f4e94b2",
        "filename": "services/net/java/android/net/apf/ApfFilter.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1185,
      "author": {
        "id": 1273909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-09T05:11:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There was a setApfVersion() method which returned true/false to signal whether the apf version was supported.\n\nDuring Jean\u0027s review, we agreed to make ApfGenerator stateless -- or rather, to configure it once at construction-time, so that you couldn\u0027t end up with a generator instance set to a non-working state.\n\nInstead of throwing from the constructor, we could do a factory method that returns null when the version is bad. Not sure what\u0027s the most idiomatic thing in Java... Probably throwing?",
      "parentUuid": "44d2c106_6068b12e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1185,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1185,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "d6846a0d80e82ac22a81b8d0426b2216386f60e5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8724f2fb_1a586353",
        "filename": "services/net/java/android/net/apf/ApfFilter.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1185,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-09T06:22:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think Lorenzo\u0027s suggestion makes sense ; emphasis on the *static* part. You would keep the version as an argument to the constructor, the constructor would still throw if the version is not supported (because there isn\u0027t much else it can do) by checking for its own static method, but the test could test for the support before it tries to create the object instead of catching.",
      "parentUuid": "13cdfdeb_5f4e94b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1185,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1185,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "d6846a0d80e82ac22a81b8d0426b2216386f60e5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
