    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54e3ebc6_8b36ebad",
        "filename": "tests/net/jni/apf_jni.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-06T13:42:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How is vendor firmware supposed to know what to pass in for data_raw? Is it always program+program_len? If so, then we should remove that argument. It\u0027s not useful, and will cause problems if the vendor firmware passes an incorrect value.\n\nAlso would suggest something more realistic: create a fixed buffer size (say, 4k), and make tha code and the data coexist in that range as opposed to passing in separate arrays.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "d6846a0d80e82ac22a81b8d0426b2216386f60e5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7a60e36_3f694181",
        "filename": "tests/net/jni/apf_jni.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1273909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-09T05:11:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed today, I\u0027ll change the interpreter call signature to\n\n  accept_packet(program_raw, program_len, memory_len, packet_raw,\n                packet_len, filter_age);\n\nwhere `memory_len` is the total buffer size (as documented in the original design doc).\n\nThe change needs to be atomic wrt to the interpreter, so I\u0027ll do it in a separate topic.",
      "parentUuid": "54e3ebc6_8b36ebad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "d6846a0d80e82ac22a81b8d0426b2216386f60e5",
